From fe2862d7ece8db26dde0653af4d5475bbfcc47f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:16:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 123/147] hydra: motion blur turned back on in a live viewport

With the renderer started while disableMotionBlur was on, unticking it
restarted the render but moving objects stayed sharp until the frame
changed or the renderer was restarted. The delegate asked for every prim to
be synced again by marking it dirty in Hydra's change tracker; in Houdini's
viewport (Hydra 2) that synced nothing. Each geometry now keeps its prim's
data source and the render index, and when the blur or the shutter changes
the render pass has every prim sample its transforms, and its instances',
again over the shutter (UpdateTransforms, shared with Sync; RefreshMotion).
Deforming points keep their samples until their next sync (K-81, checked
live through the MCP with tools/gui_capture.py).

Mesh topology is checked as it is read: face vertex counts that do not add
up to the indices, or negative ones, crashed Cycles' render threads now and
then (two runs in five); such a mesh is dropped with a warning (K-82).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
